1	/****************************************************************************
2	 * SiliconLoop - recover_task tool (M2 execution plane)
3	 *
4	 * The ONLY entry point for recovery actions (red line 7). Per the closed
5	 * loop design (docs/closed-loop-plan.md §3.1/3.2):
6	 *
7	 *   LLM proposes -> deterministic C code decides.
8	 *   The LLM only picks action (resume/restart) and target; the guards,
9	 *   the recovery ladder, the post-check and the recurrence watch all
10	 *   live here.
11	 *
12	 *   Guards (all in C, in order):
13	 *     - needs_human flag: once set (ladder exhausted), all actions refused
14	 *     - target whitelist: buggy_app / buggy_app_fixed ONLY
15	 *     - cooldown: same target once per heartbeat period (120 s)
16	 *     - hourly cap: max 6 actions per target per hour
17	 *     - mode: 0=off 1=dry-run 2=confirm 3=auto (Kconfig)
18	 *     - independent re-sample: two heartbeat reads 1.5 s apart must show
19	 *       delta == 0 before acting (a healthy task is never touched)
20	 *
21	 *   Ladder (starts where the LLM asked; escalates on failure):
22	 *     L1 resume   SIGUSR1 -> buggy_app re-enables its consumer
23	 *     L2 restart  SIGTERM + respawn the SAME workload (saved mode file),
24	 *                 so a code bug re-manifests and the ladder keeps walking
25	 *   (L3 ELF hotfix is deferred with M4; the rung above L2 is the human.)
26	 *
27	 *   Post-check: two samples 1.5 s apart, delta > 0 => recovered at that
28	 *   rung. Recurrence watch (M3): observe one more heartbeat period and
29	 *   sample again - delta == 0 means the fault came back, walk up.
30	 *   Delta == 0 right after a rung: walk up immediately.
31	 *   Ladder exhausted (L2 failed or recurred): needs_human.
32	 *
33	 *   Output: ONE line of JSON, <= 256 B (LLM request hygiene), e.g.
34	 *     {"level":1,"action":"resume","target":"buggy_app",
35	 *      "pre_delta":0,"post_delta":37,"result":"recovered"}
36	 *   result: recovered | recurred | refused | needs_confirm | dry_run
37	 *         | needs_human
38	 *   actions.log (append-only audit): timestamp,target,action,pre,post,result
39	 *
40	 * TOOL_SEC_SENSITIVE: this tool terminates/replaces real tasks. The LLM
41	 * never sees internals; strict input validation happens before anything
42	 * touches a process.
43	 ****************************************************************************/
44	
